+# @deepseek-ai/dsh-repeat-text-reminder
+
+Advisory per-agent repeat-**text** detector. It watches the assistant text an agent commits across consecutive steps of one turn and, when the same text recurs, injects a logged model context asking it to stop repeating.
+
+## Why this exists
+
+`@deepseek-ai/dsh-repeat-tool-reminder` observes `tools/post-execute`, so it only sees a loop that goes **through tool calls**. A model that emits the same plain text step after step — with no tool call — never reaches that guard, and the agent loop has no text-level loop detection of its own.
+
+The loop itself is not at fault. `packages/core/agent-loop/src/agent.ts` ends a turn as soon as a step produces no tool call:
+
+```ts
+const toolCalls = message.content.filter(block => block.type === 'tool-call')
+if (toolCalls.length === 0) return { kind: 'completed' }
+```
+
+Verified by `packages/core/agent-loop/tests/redteam-loop-termination.spec.ts`: a scripted adapter returning plain text is requested **exactly once**. Repetition therefore originates in the model's own output. This guard covers the case where the model keeps producing tool calls **and** the same narration text.
+
+## Detection is structural, not a phrase blacklist
+
+The guard compares the **normalized text** of consecutive assistant messages and counts a run:
+
+- normalization folds whitespace runs and trims; punctuation, wording, and case stay significant;
+- any content change resets the run, so repeating a word or a heading is not a loop;
+- texts shorter than `minChars` are not counted at all, so ordinary acknowledgements (`ok`, `好。`) never fire it.
+
+No specific word is ever matched. Adding a phrase to a blacklist would not fix the state cycle and would silently stop working the moment the model rephrases.
+
+## Configuration
+
+```yaml
+- id: repeat-text-reminder
+  config:
+    thresholds: [3, 5, 8]   # consecutive identical-text counts that trigger a reminder
+    minChars: 8             # minimum normalized length to count; 0 counts every non-empty text
+    textPreviewChars: 200   # cap on the text quoted in the detailed reminder
+```
+
+Misconfiguration fails loud at plugin load: an empty `thresholds` list, a non-integer, a value below 2, or a duplicate throws rather than silently falling back.
+
+## Behavior
+
+- The reminder is stamped `{ kind: 'plugin', plugin: 'repeat-text-reminder', form: 'notice' }`, so derived history renders it as a notice rather than a user prompt.
+- The first threshold delivers gentle text; later thresholds name the run length and quote the repeated text.
+- The listener always delegates (`next()`), then folds the reminder onto whatever the downstream decision was. A `reject` decision is returned unchanged.
+- A genuine user interjection resets the chain: repetition across it is not a loop.
+- Chains are keyed per Agent, so one agent repeating never trips another.
+
+## Model Experience
+
+The guard adds one `notice`-form user message to the next step's input when a run reaches a threshold. It never rewrites, blocks, or reorders the model's own output, and it adds nothing when no repetition is detected — a well-behaved turn sees zero added tokens.
+
+## Known Limitations and Deferred Work
+
+- The guard is **advisory**: it asks the model to stop, it does not terminate the turn. A model that ignores the reminder keeps running. A hard iteration cap belongs to the loop, not to an advisory reader.
+- Detection runs on `agent/pre-step`, so it observes text **after** it was committed. It cannot prevent the first repetition, only discourage the next.
+- Semantically equivalent but differently worded repetition is not detected; that would require model-side judgement, not a text comparison.
